4. Bxc4 { Pawn back, and the bishop is developed with tempo. } 4... e6
5. Nf3 { Develop and control e5. } 5... c5
6. O-O { Castle before you decide what to do in the centre. } 6... a6
7. a4 { Stop ...b5 from gaining space with tempo. } )
3. Nc3 { Develop and add pressure on d5. } 3... Nf6
4. Bg5 { Pin the knight that defends d5. } 4... Be7
5. e3 { Open the bishop and protect d4 and c4. } 5... O-O
6. Nf3 { Develop and control e5. } 6... Nbd7
7. Rc1 { The rook belongs on the c-file, which will open. } 7... c6
